config FREETZ_PACKAGE_DOMOTICZ_HOMEWIZARD_P1
	bool "Domoticz plugin: HomeWizard Wi-Fi P1 meter"
	depends on FREETZ_PACKAGE_DOMOTICZ
	default n
	help
		Extended version of the HomeWizard Wi-Fi P1 Domoticz plugin: it
		reads the P1 telegram of a HomeWizard Wi-Fi P1 meter over the
		local network (no cloud account, no HomeWizard app) and creates
		the energy devices of a smart meter installation: imported and
		exported energy, the per-tariff counters, current power per
		phase and in total, voltage and current per phase, gas and
		water, plus a few computed utility devices (daily and monthly
		totals, peak consumption, power factor and the like).

		Labels, units and the date formats of the devices follow the
		language of the hardware entry (17 translation files are
		shipped with the plugin). Only the Python standard library and
		the Domoticz module are used, so no additional Python package is
		needed.

		The plugin is installed into
		/usr/share/domoticz/plugins/HomeWizard-Wifi-p1-plugin-Extended,
		the plugin directory that Domoticz is started with (-approot of
		the domoticz package init script).

		Setup: Setup -> Hardware -> "HomeWizard P1 meter", then enter
		the IP address of the meter, the Domoticz address (127.0.0.1)
		and its HTTP port (8080); the data interval and the debug switch
		follow.

		Upstream publishes neither release tags nor a license file, so
		the build fetches a pinned commit of the main branch (the
		version of this package is that commit) and the plugin keeps the
		licensing status upstream gave it.
